{"t": 1794107788.8674903, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Regression from this change: truncating with `int()` drops a minor unit instead of rounding to the nearest one.\n\nProduction error: ReconciliationMismatch: converted totals off by 1 minor unit (expected 1100, got 1099) \u2014 https://acme.sentry.io/issues/LEDGER-WORKER-9A\n\nFirst seen in release ledger-worker@2026.11.3 (suspect commit 8c2f1d0). Fixed in worker/rates.py by restoring Decimal rounding (ROUND_HALF_UP) instead of int() truncation.", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
